A||||8||stsmithgt||Changing clutch AGAIN! .long sob story.||||8||
Z||000000||stsmithgt||08-06-2001||10:48 AM||||Last year when the tranny was out, I had the typical thought, "I might as well have the clutch changed while it's accessable".  So I had the clutch and pressure plate etc. that the shop recommended installed.  I thought my troubles were over.  Weekend before last my car became stubborn to shift coming off the freeway.  I thought it felt funny when I was getting on the road, but then thought it was just me.  Anyway, it got extremely difficult to shift within a block from the first time I had to stop since getting off the freeway some 20 miles later.  I pulled it into a parking lot basically stuck in first gear because I could feel something in the clutch system was giving or gave out.  After I stopped I tried to shift into first gear, but there was something definately wrong with the clutch and it wouldn't go.  With it running I started to get out to take a look under the hood.  I immediately shut off the engine off because when I opened the door I heard metal rattling and scraping coming from the engine compartment. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR><B>I'M STRANDED...</B><BR>In Sacramento at 10:00 p.m..  I was on my way over to a buddies house to take advantage of his jaccuzi since my back was killing me.  Now I'm in more pain because I'm pissed off. I'm thinking that a system I paid a lot of money for has failed leaving me stranded. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <BR>This is where friends become important.  I borrowed a truck from a buddy to get back home down near Monterey.  My car is so much more comfortable than that toyota truck, but I didn't mention that to him.<BR>I still don't have my car back since they couldn't finish by the weekend so I'll go back up to Sac. next weekend to pick it up.  These extra expences have literally drained my account (along with everybody else that wanted money last month). <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I have to  make a lot of sacrifices to save money now.  I hate having to change my budjet.<BR>I have a couple valid theories on what failed and why, but I want to see the parts before I make my conclusion.  WELL, that's my sob story.  I'd be crying in my beer, but I quit drinking a couple of months ago.  I didn't drink for self pitty anyway so no big deal.  I'm sure I'll have more to say, as if this isn't enough, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> when I get my car and it's former guts back.  Until then, I hope no moore trouble comes along because I don't think I'll tolerate so easily. LATER!!!!<P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Bluebottlejunky||08-06-2001||12:16 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I hope my clucth never goes out! Good luck dude<BR><P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bruce||08-06-2001||01:25 PM||||My clutch is ready for replacement after only 10,000 miles; either bad parts (NAPA), a bad mechanic, or both. Hope the next time around goes better for you. <BR>My sister lives in Pacific Grove, so let me know if you find a good mechanic.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||08-06-2001||02:23 PM||||Hey Bruce,<BR>A good mechanic around here? Hah! At least not for a Fiero that I've found yet. Plus it's expensive as hell down here.  I think the mechanics like to feed on stranded tourists or just blame their prices on high overhead.  I've tried about five places down here and a couple of them a couple times at first not believing a large shop could be so bad at problem solving in one visit.  I guess I like learning the hard way. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>I'm keeping my eyes open for a good shop, but nothing else I've checked out so far has been impressive.  <BR>I did find a tire center through my brother called, Monterey Tire Center.  Paul is the boss hog there.  I had him put on new tires, shocks, struts and alignment.  They did a nice job and took care of my car fairly quick though I told them to take there time like I tell most of the mechanics I've had work on it.  I usually explain my expectations before they start so if something goes wrong they know where I'll be coming from.  <BR>My car is at a shop up in Sacramento where I have a friend that's the service manager.  He makes sure the jobs done right the first time before I get my car back.  The price is fair too.  I expect to pick up my GT next weekend though it's probably going to be done today.  The last couple times something broke, the ignition switch linkage and my clutch, luckily I happened to be in Sacramento at the time within 5 miles of his shop!  I'm up there a lot since I'm originaly from Davis so I have friends up there I visit, like the one that loan me his truck.  I'd like to move back up there away from this cold, foggy, tourist infested money hole, but I have to find work up there first.  <P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bruce||08-06-2001||02:40 PM||||I had my clutch replaced in El Granada (near Half Moon Bay), and the mark-up there was pretty high, too. It's amazing what some people in Nor. Cal get away with! Makes you a little cynical sometimes. Fortunately, my faith in people is restored here on the forum.<BR>b||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||08-06-2001||03:01 PM||||I hear you on the cynical part.  I was trying to decide which way I wanted to repair an exhaust leak when this all happened.  I don't think I can swing getting both the clutch AND the exhaust fixed at the same time.  It's too expensive even with fair prices.  That's probably why I'm so bent about having to do my clutch again.  There's always something else that needs fixing.  I don't need things I've had fixed already failing in an unusually short time.  I don't thrash my car it's too expensive to.  Besides, I got most of that out of my system when I was younger.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||08-06-2001||04:12 PM||||Make sure it is a new clutch and not a remanufactured deal!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bruce||08-06-2001||04:34 PM||||After all the fuss I've heard over the Kevlar clutch, I'm going with the Centerforce super-duper model. That should last awhile, especially since I only put a couple of thousand miles a year on my 86 GT.||||reg||1
Z||000008||stsmithgt||08-06-2001||05:55 PM||||I don't think it's the disk itself that failed, but I want to see the parts to see what and where exactly it failed to determine what happened and hopefully why.  Like I said, I do have a theory or two.  I have other people fix my car for me because because I don't have a place to do the work and my back would give me hell if I did it myself especially if I was in a hurry.  If I had a second vehicle, I probably would have taken my time and fixed it at a buddies house in his garage on the weekends, but I don't so I have to deal with other people to do the work.  It CAN get frustrating.||||reg||1
